    {
      "id": "claim_3853a144637f493ba567245ca57f4a45",
      "statement": "Two VS Code-specific behaviors break a privileged DinD container on Docker Desktop + WSL2: the Wayland-socket bind-mount (fixed by setting dev.containers.mountWaylandSocket: false in VS Code User settings) and the Docker credential-helper injection (already fixed in committed config via containerEnv.DOCKER_CONFIG=/home/coder/.docker-dind).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer.md#L113-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cbfadf507871eaefd106afb2d93651e82add9bbd3cb2e685793bee302c8d10d1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3ea4c8e357684f0c9c56bdc7ee6f38b4",
      "statement": "Host env vars forwarded into the devcontainer via ${localEnv} (MCM_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, MCM_DEVCONTAINER_IMAGE, FORGE_REGISTRY_HOST, TMDB_API_KEY, MCM_FORGE_TOKEN, MCM_FORGE_ISSUE_TOKEN) are read from the VS Code process environment at launch time; setx alone is not enough — VS Code must be fully quit and relaunched with the value already present, then the container recreated.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer.md#L134-L139",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f8e42df6dd922df15df34258b8246e68eeb981b6ddee251b2bbb17f0765d2346:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c488ca1052694035bf10588a2a428cdb",
      "statement": "MCM_DEVCONTAINER_IMAGE is required under VS Code — the ${localEnv:VAR:default} fallback default is NOT applied by the VS Code Dev Containers extension; with the var unset, VS Code passes --build-arg BASE_IMAGE= (empty) and the build fails. The headless @devcontainers/cli does apply the default.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer.md#L1072-L1088",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7b093a0f6499d932241ec2424b7b282f304f3a8c963b3d8c0d77e3a5ecf6c1de:"
