    {
      "id": "claim_8a2598a7acf5407abc2ec7c6ac366a8b",
      "statement": "Docker won't start after a devcontainer rebuild when a previous container instance is still running; its containerd holds an flock on the DinD volume's meta.db, blocking the new daemon indefinitely. Diagnosis: python3 flock probe distinguishes locked (recoverable) from corrupt (destructive). Fix: docker rm -f every other container, then sudo nohup /usr/local/share/docker-init.sh. Do NOT delete meta.db or docker volume rm — meta.db deletion destroys all DinD images, and /workspaces is a named volume so a prune removes the working tree.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer.md#L438-L494",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6f231089d9d1d01f1232df0f09ef514642223163ee7b905595ec9365ae14fc09:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2027bdc40ec3436097fad37fda90e724",
      "statement": "Editing a file under node_modules/ writes into the pnpm content-addressed store because node_modules entries are hardlinks into it; files with identical content share one inode across package versions. A per-file backup-then-patch loop corrupts its own backups (the store entry changes with the first write), and pnpm install does not re-verify store content hashes so corruption outlives a reinstall. Safe procedure: stat -c '%h %i' first, record clean md5sum, patch one path, then verify with md5 and pnpm store status.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer.md#L1127-L1172",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:725c30b96178d4343f7ffba1459cf07d9b5afd59252d9bff9376f1b5a4338a76:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6f2dd1f6c2824a0ebed12c5def9aaf63",
      "statement": "Multiple Claude sessions share one devcontainer and one checkout; git operations in /workspaces/mcm are visible to all sessions. Branch work must use a git worktree under /home/coder/worktrees/<slug>. The node_modules symlink from the worktree to the main checkout is sufficient for node --test and scripts/*.mjs gates but causes ERR_PNPM_UNSAFE_MODULES_DIR for any pnpm nx target — a real pnpm install in the worktree is the only fix (~4 min). Worktrees do not survive a container rebuild.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/devcontainer.md#L303-L404",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:611fc7bfb038da642d83d6108f65b770633a995f93f12e91d8599e354c8e4f56:"
        }
      ]
    },
